cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research project, please cite the author and manuscript."
title: "Initial Valuation-One Cylinders in the Accelerated Syracuse Map"
authors:
  - family-names: Lubuimi
    given-names: Ta-Yoshua
date-released: 2026-11-10
version: "0.1.0"
type: article
abstract: >-
  An independent exposition and Lean formalization of the classical parity-vector
  congruence classification for initial valuation-one runs in accelerated Syracuse
  orbits, with exact run length, natural densities, and a signed-offset margin.
  The companion finite valuation-word cylinder statement is likewise framed as a
  classical parity-vector consequence, not as a novelty or priority claim.
keywords:
  - Collatz conjecture
  - Syracuse dynamics
  - 2-adic valuation
  - residue cylinders
  - affine offset identity
repository-code: "https://github.com/s4ztz4bnf6-maker/Lubuimi"
